@startuml seq-structure-headings
!theme plain
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam responseMessageBelowArrow true
skinparam maxMessageSize 210
skinparam wrapWidth 190
skinparam shadowing false
title Structure headings — one completion per unheaded chapter\n(spec: flows.spec.ts · "structure generation + language check flows")
' Aliases match docs/specs/component-map.puml.

actor User
participant "PAGE_CHAT\nChatComponent" as PAGE
participant "ORCH_RUNNER\nLlmFlowRunner" as RUN
participant "flows/structure\nstructureHeadings()" as ST
participant "SVC_TREE\nreader · writer" as TREE
participant "ORCH_TRANSPORT\ntextCompletion()" as TR
participant "PORT\nChatApiPort" as API

== 1. Which chapters are in scope? ==
User -> PAGE : "Add chapter headings"
PAGE -> RUN : run({node, usecase:'structure-headings'})
RUN -> ST : structureHeadings(env)
ST -> TREE : getActivePath().filter(role === 'assistant' && content)
note right of ST
  scope = the ACTIVE PATH only. Off-path branches never get a
  heading — that is the difference to structure-title, which
  reads every assistant node of the chat.
  (chat.component.spec: "generates a heading for each assistant
  node on the active path".)
end note
ST -> ST : previous = []   (chapters already headed, in order)

== 2. One completion per chapter, in story order ==
loop each assistant node on the path
  alt two stop conditions
    ST -> ST : env.signal.aborted?  → break (hard Stop)
    ST -> ST : shouldStopAfterCurrentStep()? → break\n("Finish & stop")
    note right of ST
      graceful stop is checked BEFORE the request, so the chapter
      being generated is still fetched and PERSISTED.
    end note
  end
  alt the chapter already hangs under a structural node
    ST -> ST : previous.push({node, heading})\ncontinue  (no completion!)
    note right of ST
      flows.spec "skips chapters that already have a heading but
      keeps them in context": exactly ONE completion for 2 chapters.
    end note
  else unheaded chapter
    ST -> ST : blocks = previous chapters WITH their headings\n + current chapter "(to be created)"
    ST -> TR : complete(instruction + blocks + 'Return only the heading text.')
    TR -> API : /proxy completion (non-streaming)
    TR --> ST : slots.text
    ST -> ST : headingContent = text.trim()\nempty ⇒ error slot, run ends
    == 3. Wrap the chapter under the new heading ==
    ST -> TREE : addStructureNode(chatId, assistant.parentId, headingContent)
    TREE -> API : createNode(role:'structural')
    ST -> TREE : reparentNodes([assistant.id], heading.id)
    ST -> TREE : setActiveChild(parent, heading)\nsetActiveChild(heading, assistant)
    note right of TREE
      net effect asserted by flows.spec:
      heading.parentId = q1, a1.parentId = heading.id,
      getActiveChild(q1) = heading, getActiveChild(heading) = a1.
      structure-heading (singular) instead PATCHES an existing
      structural parent rather than adding a second one.
    end note
    ST -> ST : previous.push({node, heading})\ncreatedIds.push(heading.id)
  end
end

== 4. Result ==
ST --> RUN : flow{structureNodeId: last, structureNodeIds: createdIds}
RUN --> PAGE : slots
note right of PAGE
  flows.spec: 2 chapters without headings ⇒ 2 fetches, 2 structural
  nodes, structureNodeIds.length === 2.
  chat.component.spec: "provides previous chapters incl. their
  headings as context for the last one" — the second request body
  contains Answer one, "First Heading" and Answer two.
end note

@enduml
